Fixes Issues:
-------------
- Fixes provided by OpenSTLinux v4.1.1 and v4.1.2:
    * Update to Yocto Project 4.0.19 (2022-04.19-kirkstone)
    * Update to Linux Kernel 5.15.145
    * BSP maturation with an amount of 66 fixes delivered in the following BSP components:
	TF-A, u-Boot, OP-TEE and Linux Kernel

    For more details on those fixes, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note_-_v4.1.0
       * OpenSTLinux v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note_-_v4.1.0

- Fixes provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
    * eMMC clock frequency was only 31.25 MHz:
	Internal CPU clock tree has been changed so that eMMC and SD-card clock frequency is now 50Mhz.
    * SD-card clock frequency was limited to 10Mhz:
	Remove this limitation set in device tree. SD-card clock frequency is now 50Mhz.
    * SDK build failure:
        SDK build was failing because of a yocto fetch error (cmsis-svd recipe).
	Fetch URL is corrected so that SDK can build again.

Features:
---------
- New features provided by OpenSTLinux v4.1.1 and v4.1.2:
    For more details on those new features, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note_-_v4.1.0
       * OpenSTLinux v4.1.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v4/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note_-_v4.1.0

- New features provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
     * add OP-TEE support (not activated by default). Only SP-MIN was supported before.
     * add RAUC support for BSP update solution (https://rauc.io/)
     * add FIT image support (https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/How_to_create_Signed_FIT_image_from_Distribution_package)
     * Support new AC158 7” LCD display (ILITEK ILI2130 capacitive touch screen instead of EDT FT5x06 touch)
     * RTC settings like Backup Switchover Mode are now configured over hwclock and not device tree any more

     Please note that the TF-A firmware update feature is not enabled anymore by default. This feature is enabled
     only when using our rauc distro. But you can enabled it if necessary without using rauc, just adding the following
     machine feature in your machine.conf file:
     MACHINE_FEATURES += "fw-update"

- Existing features (from PD23.1.0 PHYTEC BSP release):
  * Boot support:
    * Boot from SD-card / eMMC / NAND / NOR-eMMC (Linux boot on eMMC)

  * Flash devices support:
    * eMMC (u-boot/kernel)
    * NAND (u-boot/kernel)
    * SPI NOR (u-boot/kernel)
    * SD-card (u-boot/kernel)

  * phyBOARD-Sargas addons support:
    * PEB-AV-01 support (HDMI module)
    * PEB-AV-02 with AC158 EDT 7" capacitive touch screen display support
    * MB1407 MIPI DSI screen support (4" touch screen display from STMicroelectronics)
    * Raspberry Pi 7" Touch Screen MIPI DSI Display support (touch screen is not functional)
    * PEB-WLBT-05 (2.4Ghz and 5Ghz version) support (WLAN/Bluetooth expansion)
    * "RedBear IoT pHAT v1.0" support (WLAN/Bluetooth Raspberry Pi HAT solution)
    * phyCAM-P VM-016 BW & COL

  * Peripherals suppotrt:
    * I2C (u-boot/kernel)
    * UARTs (u-boot/kernel)
    * RS485 (kernel)
    * EEPROM (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-Host (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-OTG (u-boot/kernel)
    * Ethernet - 100Mpbs/1Gbps (u-boot/kernel)
    * CAN FD (kernel)
    * SPI (kernel)
    * Audio codec support (Line IN/OUT, Headphone) - TLV320AIC3007 (kernel)
    * RTC - RV-3028-C7 (kernel)
    * LED dimmer - PCA9533/01 (kernel)
    * User buttons support (kernel)
    * TIMERs (kernel)
    * ADCs (kernel)


Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
STM32CubeMP1 (Cortex-M4):
  * OpenAMP compilation issue with MDK-ARM when code generated through CubeMx:
    To avoid compiling errors in OpenAMP when compiling in MDK-ARM IDE, you have to disable the « Use MicroLIB » in « Target » tab.
